{
  "name": "Haulmark",
  "category": "Business dashboards",
  "kind": "template",
  "summary": "A fleet and delivery dashboard with a drawn road map where trucks move along their routes",
  "about": "A nine-page dispatch room for a trucking company, on a deep navy canvas with sand cards and one signal-yellow accent. The live map is drawn as a road atlas: trucks drive their routes with ETA labels that tick down, and any trip opens on a timeline you can scrub to replay it. Drivers, vehicles, loads with signed proof of delivery, fuel, alerts and reports all work and keep their changes.",
  "how": [
    "Open a page from the top bar; the little truck under the menu drives to the page you pick",
    "On the live map, click a truck to follow it, filter by moving, late or parked, and switch traffic, fuel stops or ETA labels",
    "Open a trip and drag the timeline handle, use the arrow keys or press play to replay it on the map",
    "Plan a trip, reassign a driver, book a service or add a fill-up; every form checks what you type",
    "Drag a load across the board, and sign for a delivery on the signature pad to create its proof of delivery",
    "Acknowledge, assign or resolve alerts and switch alert rules on or off",
    "Press Ctrl+K to jump to a page, truck or driver; change units or reset the demo data in Settings"
  ],
